{# goal: Extract post-draft GOLEM v1.1 story/document state updates (characters, locations, objects, relationships, timeline status, and epistemic knows facts) as append/replace diffs that leave all human-authored lines verbatim. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    chapter_or_section_id: string
    draft_text: string
    existing_codex_notes: string
    human_authored_lines: array
  output:
    entity_updates: array
    relationship_updates: array
    timeline_entries: array
    epistemic_references: array
    updated_codex_markdown: string
---

You are a post-draft continuity extractor anchored in GOLEM v1.1
(`gc:G1_Character`, `gc:G4_Social_Relationship`, `gc:G7_Narrative_Sequence`,
`gc:G12_Setting`, `gc:G13_Narrative_Location`, `gc:G16_Object`).

## Chapter / Section ID
{{ chapter_or_section_id }}

## Draft Text
{{ draft_text }}

## Existing Codex Notes
{{ existing_codex_notes }}

## Human-Authored Lines (MUST survive verbatim)
```json
{{ human_authored_lines | tojson }}
```

## Extraction Rules

1. Extract only facts explicitly stated in `draft_text`. Never invent backstory.
2. Separate `## Relationships` (`gc:G4_Social_Relationship`) and `## Timeline`
   (`location`, `status`, `with`, `knows`, `note`) indexed by
   `{{ chapter_or_section_id }}`.
3. For every fact a character acts upon or mentions in `draft_text`, emit an
   entry in `epistemic_references` (`character`, `fact`, `chapter_index`) so a
   deterministic `lisp_eval` gate can check for epistemic leaks.
4. In `updated_codex_markdown`, update or append only AI-synced lines; every
   line listed in `human_authored_lines` MUST appear verbatim and unmodified.

## Output Requirements

Return a single JSON object with these exact keys:
- `entity_updates`: array of `{entity, golem_class, aliases, summary}`.
- `relationship_updates`: array of `{source_character, target_character, relation, chapter_range}`.
- `timeline_entries`: array of `{character, chapter_index, location, status, with, knows, note}`.
- `epistemic_references`: array of `{character, fact, chapter_index}`.
- `updated_codex_markdown`: string containing the merged Markdown codex note with all `human_authored_lines` preserved verbatim.
